The `rate` pod's CPU and memory are flat or lower during the incident, so it is not saturated. The delay sits on the `search → rate` connection. I have enough to answer.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "rate",
      "fault_kind": "network_delay",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT count(*) n, round(approx_quantile(epoch_ms(s.time)-epoch_ms(c.time),0.5),1) AS server_start_gap_ms_p50, round(approx_quantile(c.duration/1e6,0.5),1) AS client_ms_p50, round(approx_quantile(s.duration/1e6,0.5),2) AS server_ms_p50 FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON c.trace_id=s.trace_id AND s.parent_span_id=c.span_id WHERE c.service_name='search' AND c.span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' AND s.attr_span_kind='Server'",
          "claim": "search to rate GetRates: client waits about 1.9 s, but rate's server span starts about 1.5 s late and runs in about 0.5 ms."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT count(*) n, round(approx_quantile(c.duration/1e6,0.5),1) AS client_ms_p50, round(approx_quantile(s.duration/1e6,0.5),2) AS server_ms_p50 FROM normal_traces c JOIN normal_traces s ON c.trace_id=s.trace_id AND s.parent_span_id=c.span_id WHERE c.service_name='search' AND c.span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' AND s.attr_span_kind='Server'",
          "claim": "In the normal period the same search to rate call takes about 2 ms end to end, with the server span at about 1.5 ms."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, metric, round(avg(value),5) AS avg_v, round(max(value),5) AS max_v FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE service_name='rate' AND metric IN ('container.cpu.usage','container.memory.working_set') GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "rate's CPU and memory stay low during the incident, so the pod is not saturated and the delay is not in rate's own work."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "rate",
      "to": "search",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.service_name AS caller, s.service_name AS callee, count(*) n, round(approx_quantile(c.duration/1e6,0.5),1) AS call_ms_p50 FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON c.trace_id=s.trace_id AND s.parent_span_id=c.span_id WHERE c.service_name='search' AND s.service_name='rate' AND c.attr_span_kind='Client' AND s.attr_span_kind='Server' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "The slow rate calls are made by search, which waits about 1.8 s per GetRates call."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.service_name AS caller, s.service_name AS callee, count(*) n, round(approx_quantile(c.duration/1e6,0.5),1) AS client_ms_p50, round(approx_quantile(s.duration/1e6,0.5),1) AS server_ms_p50 FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON c.trace_id=s.trace_id AND s.parent_span_id=c.span_id WHERE c.service_name='frontend' AND s.service_name='search' AND c.attr_span_kind='Client' AND s.attr_span_kind='Server' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "frontend's search.Search/Nearby calls take about 1.9 s, matching search's own server span, so search's slowness is passed up to frontend."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

